      "errors": [],
      "result": "Optional Subject Selection Tool\n\nAnswer honestly about your background, time and preferences. The tool validates FPSC grouping rules and suggests combinations with reasons and risks - it does not predict scores.\n\n1\nBackground\n2\nTime & skills\n3\nInterests\n4\nPreferences\n5\nResults\nSubject selection is a personal academic decision. Previous scoring trends do not guarantee future marks.\n\nChoose exactly 600 optional marks within the group limits; you do not need a subject from every group. Check the official FPSC syllabus and the rules for your examination year before applying.\n\nSuggested combination\nValid - 600/600 marks\nPublic Administration (Group 3)\n100\nGender Studies (Group 5)\n100\nSociology (Group 7)\n100\nPolitical Science (Group 1)\n200\nHistory of Pakistan & India (Group 4)\n100\n\nWhy these: chosen for alignment with your background and interests, overlap with compulsory subjects, your available 6 months, and your comfort profile.\n\nRisks: Low structural risk; depth of preparation still decides the outcome.\n\nUse these in my study planner\nAlternative combination\nValid - 600/600 marks\nInternational Relations (Group 1)\n200\nGovernance & Public Policies (Group 3)\n100\nIslamic History & Culture (Group 4)\n100\nEnvironmental Sciences (Group 5)\n100\nConstitutional Law (Group 6)\n100\n\nWhy these: chosen for alignment with your background and interests, overlap with compulsory subjects, your available 6 months, and your comfort profile.\n\nRisks: Constitutional Law: Requires accurate citation of constitutions\n\nUse these in my study planner\nBack\nStart over"
    },
